From 552306a015aede9e50218ddc6f97e4aaeae3dc3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 14:23:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0066 -- audio-thread hard-park (486
 quit-hang fix proper)

486-class campaign Bug 2 final fix. The marker iters (SDL_mixer/0002 +
SDL/0065, flush-instr #75, 486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md sec.16)
pinned the quit-to-DOS hang to a lock/scheduler race INSIDE
ObtainLogicalAudioDevice (SDL_audio.c) during the simplified-stream
device close that SDL_DestroyAudioStream(mixer->output_stream)
triggers via SDL_CloseAudioDevice during MIX_DestroyMixer teardown.
Both DX2-66 cells wedge there; the audio playback thread is alive
throughout, cycling device->lock + output_stream->lock each Iterate.
Deterministic on the Intel 486DX2; the Am5x86 and Pentium dodge it.

A focused source read of ObtainLogicalAudioDevice does not pin the
exact stuck line -- each lock resolves in the static model; the bug
is a cooperative-scheduler / lock-race timing pattern not visible
statically. So this is a targeted defensive fix at the precisely-named
stage (defensive_rewrite_requires_identified_failure_stage), not a
line-level repair.

Fix: remove the cross-thread race entirely by parking the SDL audio
playback thread OUT of the lock-contention window during the
teardown. The engine already calls SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown() at
snd-shutdown[3.5/6] -- BEFORE MIX_DestroyMixer, on main, single-
threaded, no race -- the right hook. Patch 0066 makes that call
flip a new module-scope flag g_dos_audio_hard_park = true. Then
DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice, at the top of its loop (right after the
existing SDL/0046 device->shutdown bail), sees the flag and
SDL_Delay(5)+continues. So the audio thread parks INSIDE WaitDevice,
which runs OUTSIDE device->lock per SDL_audio.c's
while(Iterate()){WaitDevice();} structure -- holding NO contended
locks, never re-entering Iterate. Main's SDL_DestroyAudioStream
(mixer->output_stream) -> SDL_CloseAudioDevice -> ObtainLogicalAudioDevice
then runs with zero audio-thread lock contention; the race is gone.
When main's ClosePhysicalAudioDevice eventually sets device->shutdown
= 1, WaitDevice's existing SDL/0046 bail (checked at the top of every
loop iteration, before the park check) fires, the Iterate loop
observes shutdown, the thread exits, the join completes, CloseDevice
runs ("audio close:" lines emit), MIX_DestroyMixer returns, quit
completes.

Crucially the fix does NOT set device->shutdown early -- that would
create a SerializePhysicalDeviceClose deadlock (its
while(shutdown)WaitCondition spin waits for a close_cond broadcast
that only ClosePhysicalAudioDevice itself issues; setting shutdown
early wedges main's own teardown). Park bypasses that trap by leaving
shutdown alone and instead removing the audio thread from the
lock-contention window via the WaitDevice loop. It also does not
touch any SDL-core lock (subsystem_rwlock, device->lock,
output_stream->lock, close_cond) -- entirely SDL-DOS-backend lane.

Audio is already silenced at SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown time (Organya
shutdown ran at snd-shutdown[2/6], Pixtone at [3/6]), so parking the
audio thread is lossless behaviorally. SDL_Delay(5) in the park loop
yields cooperatively, so main runs freely during the park.

The earlier SDL/0063 WaitDevice ring-drain backstop guards a different
(latent) deadlock and stays as is. Patch 0066 sits at WaitDevice's
top, before SDL/0063's part-1/part-2; under park, the loop returns
from SDL_Delay+continue before reaching SDL/0063's code.

Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_SHUTDOWN_PARK (default-ON,
strict-"0"). =0 makes SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown skip the flag flip,
so WaitDevice never parks -- pre-0066 behavior, used for the
operator's DX2 A/B reproducer cell. Resolved once at OpenDevice;
cached. Boot banner emits the active state. Documented in
docs/internal/BOOT.md; banner regex added to
tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh BANNERS.

One TU touched (vendor/SDL/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c); minor
edits (~70 lines): two new statics, an OpenDevice killswitch resolve
block, the SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown setter, and the WaitDevice park
check. Rides the next combined DX2-66 iter (DX2-66-only per
486_iteration_workflow). Independent of nx 0161.

Workspace-local per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md; never upstreamed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 134 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 134 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 3d74628cc..04a1b266d 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -202,6 +202,63 @@ static Uint64 g_c_audiocb_total_ns = 0;    /* summed callback wall-clock, curren
 static Uint64 g_c_audiocb_max_ns = 0;      /* worst single callback, current block */
 static Uint32 g_c_audiocb_block = 0;       /* emitted-block counter */
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0066): audio-thread hard-park
+   coordination for the quit-to-DOS teardown.
+
+   486-class campaign Bug 2 was pinned by patches SDL_mixer/0002 +
+   SDL/0065 to a lock/scheduler race INSIDE ObtainLogicalAudioDevice
+   (SDL_audio.c) during the simplified-output_stream device close that
+   SDL_DestroyAudioStream(mixer->output_stream) triggers via
+   SDL_CloseAudioDevice -- main wedges there while the cooperative
+   audio playback thread is alive and cycling device->lock /
+   output_stream->lock each Iterate. Deterministic on the Intel
+   486DX2; the Am5x86-133 and the Pentium OverDrive dodge it (flush-
+   instr #75, 486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md sec.16).
+
+   This patch removes the race rather than patching SDL-core locks.
+   `g_dos_audio_hard_park` is flipped true by `SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown`
+   (already engine-called at snd-shutdown[3.5/6], BEFORE
+   MIX_DestroyMixer, on the main thread, single-threaded -- no race).
+   `DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice`, at the top of its loop, sees the flag
+   and SDL_Delay(5)+continues -- parking the audio thread in WaitDevice
+   (which runs OUTSIDE device->lock per SDL_audio.c's
+   `while(Iterate()){WaitDevice();}` structure), holding NO contended
+   locks, never re-entering Iterate. main's SDL_DestroyAudioStream
+   -> SDL_CloseAudioDevice -> ObtainLogicalAudioDevice then runs with
+   zero audio-thread lock contention; the race is gone. When main's
+   ClosePhysicalAudioDevice sets device->shutdown=1, WaitDevice's
+   existing SDL/0046 bail (checked at the top of every loop iteration,
+   before the park check) fires immediately, the Iterate loop observes
+   shutdown=1, the thread exits, the join completes, CloseDevice runs
+   ("audio close:" lines emit), MIX_DestroyMixer returns, quit completes.
+
+   Audio is already silenced at SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown time (Organya
+   shutdown ran at snd-shutdown[2/6], Pixtone at [3/6]), so parking the
+   audio thread loses nothing behaviorally.
+
+   Critically, this does NOT set device->shutdown early -- that would
+   create a SerializePhysicalDeviceClose deadlock (its `while(shutdown)
+   WaitCondition` spin waits for a close_cond broadcast that only
+   ClosePhysicalAudioDevice itself issues; setting shutdown early
+   wedges main's own teardown). Park bypasses that trap by leaving
+   shutdown alone and instead removing the audio thread from the
+   lock-contention window via the WaitDevice loop.
+
+   Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_SHUTDOWN_PARK=0 disables the
+   park (g_dos_audio_shutdown_park_disabled true). With the killswitch
+   set, SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown does NOT flip g_dos_audio_hard_park,
+   so WaitDevice never parks -- pre-0066 behavior, used for the
+   operator's DX2 A/B to reproduce the original hang. Default ON.
+   Strict-"0" match per CLAUDE.md env-var convention. Resolved once
+   at OpenDevice; cached.
+
+   g_dos_audio_hard_park is volatile -- main thread (SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown)
+   writes it; audio thread (WaitDevice) reads it. Aligned bool stores
+   are atomic on x86 (DJGPP target), matching the existing audio-flag
+   pattern (g_dos_audio_resume_request, g_dos_audio_pause_request). */
+static bool g_dos_audio_shutdown_park_disabled = false;
+static volatile bool g_dos_audio_hard_park = false;
+
 /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0058): Shape A mechanism-histogram
    instrumentation state. Diagnostic backstop for wave-36 PLAY6 Shape
    D fps lever per `pressure_test_tidy_narratives.md` discipline: if
@@ -762,6 +819,35 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
             return true;
         }
 
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0066): hard-park gate.
+           SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown flips g_dos_audio_hard_park=true on
+           the main thread at snd-shutdown[3.5/6], BEFORE
+           MIX_DestroyMixer, single-threaded -- no race. When parked,
+           the audio thread SDL_Delay-loops here at the top of
+           WaitDevice -- OUTSIDE the Iterate's device->lock per
+           SDL_audio.c's `while(Iterate()){WaitDevice();}` structure --
+           holding NO contended locks, never re-entering Iterate. main's
+           SDL_DestroyAudioStream(mixer->output_stream) ->
+           SDL_CloseAudioDevice -> ObtainLogicalAudioDevice then runs
+           with zero audio-thread lock contention, removing the
+           486DX2 quit-hang race (486-class campaign Bug 2 / flush-instr
+           #75, 486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md sec.16). The park exits
+           via the SDL/0046 shutdown bail above on the next loop
+           iteration once main's ClosePhysicalAudioDevice sets
+           device->shutdown=1. SDL_Delay(5) yields cooperatively, so
+           main runs freely during the park (the DOS_Yield baked into
+           SDL_Delay schedules main once per 5 ms wall-clock).
+           Killswitched at OpenDevice via
+           SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_SHUTDOWN_PARK=0 -- the setter in
+           SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown is gated on the killswitch, so
+           with =0 the flag never flips true and this check stays
+           false; pre-0066 behavior preserved for the operator's DX2
+           A/B reproducer cell. */
+        if (g_dos_audio_hard_park) {
+            SDL_Delay(5);
+            continue;
+        }
+
         /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0038): service pause/resume
            requests on each WaitDevice loop iteration. Pause requests
            come from the IRQ handler (consecutive-silent-IRQ threshold
@@ -989,6 +1075,31 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
         }
     }
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0066): resolve the audio-thread
+       hard-park killswitch once at OpenDevice time. Strict-"0" match
+       per CLAUDE.md env-var convention. Cached at module scope; read
+       by SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown (which gates the
+       g_dos_audio_hard_park flag flip on it). Default ON: it removes
+       the cross-thread lock/scheduler race in ObtainLogicalAudioDevice
+       the 486-class campaign surfaced on the Intel 486DX2 configs
+       (docs/internal/486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md sec.16, Bug 2). */
+    {
+        const char *park_hint = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_SHUTDOWN_PARK");
+        g_dos_audio_shutdown_park_disabled =
+            (park_hint && park_hint[0] == '0' && park_hint[1] == 0);
+        if (g_dos_audio_shutdown_park_disabled) {
+            doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_SHUTDOWN_PARK=0 "
+                             "(SDL/0066 audio-thread hard-park DISABLED; "
+                             "SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown will not park; A/B-only -- "
+                             "reproduces pre-0066 quit hang on real DX2)");
+        } else {
+            doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0066 audio-thread hard-park active "
+                             "(default; teardown lock-handoff guard; "
+                             "SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown will park audio thread "
+                             "in WaitDevice before MIX_DestroyMixer device close)");
+        }
+    }
+
     /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0064): resolve the SFX-stall
        instrumentation part-C gate once at OpenDevice time. Reuses the
        existing FINE_INSTR env var (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FINE_INSTR,
@@ -1417,6 +1528,29 @@ void SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown(void)
         doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown — gate already "
                          "disabled (killswitch or repeat call); no-op");
     }
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0066): set the hard-park flag so
+       DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice parks the audio thread OUT of the
+       lock-contention window during the MIX_DestroyMixer teardown
+       that follows. Gated on the killswitch resolved at OpenDevice
+       via SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_SHUTDOWN_PARK. Without this
+       park, ObtainLogicalAudioDevice -- reached via SDL_DestroyAudioStream
+       (mixer->output_stream)'s simplified-stream device close --
+       wedges on real Intel 486DX2 hardware (486-class campaign Bug 2,
+       486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md sec.16). This is the actual
+       quit-hang fix; the earlier SDL/0063 WaitDevice ring-drain
+       backstop guards a different (latent) deadlock and stays as is.
+       Same caller, single-threaded -- this runs on main BEFORE
+       MIX_DestroyMixer, so flipping the flag here cannot race the
+       audio thread's read. */
+    if (!g_dos_audio_shutdown_park_disabled && !g_dos_audio_hard_park) {
+        g_dos_audio_hard_park = true;
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0066 hard-park ENGAGED -- "
+                         "DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice will SDL_Delay-loop "
+                         "outside device->lock until device->shutdown is set, "
+                         "removing the audio-thread race with main's "
+                         "SDL_DestroyAudioStream(output_stream) teardown");
+    }
 }
 
 // Return the staging buffer. The SDL audio pipeline writes the mixed audio
-- 
